<EasyInstall>
    <Name>Just Get The Loot Already!</Name>
    <Author>fuhq2mofo</Author>
    <Version>1.9.1 - rebuilt</Version>
    <Link>https://www.nexusmods.com/reddeadredemption2/mods/1958</Link>
    <Metadata />

    <!-- Not the files of the download (those are in ../original). Both files here are the files
         of game build 1.0.1491.50 with these changes only:
         - lootconfigdata.meta: three new rate selectors at 2.0, used by body looting, plant and
           egg picking and dead-horse saddlebags (FAST_LOOT), by the swipe and placeholder
           skinning sets (FAST_SWIPE_SKINNING) and by the skinning scenes of each species, small
           animals and birds (FAST_SCENE_SKINNING). Change the one Default value of a selector
           to tune its group
         - lootconfigdata.meta: 17 carriable species (deer, buck, pronghorn, ram, boar, pig,
           javelina, wolves, cougar, panther, coyote, fox, beaver, goat, small alligator) are
           skinned with the swipe set the game itself keeps as their fallback, which gives the
           same pelt. Animals created by a script (missions, legendary hunts) are left out
         - humaninteraction.meta: AnimRate 2.0 on Interaction_LootSaddleBags (saddlebags of a
           standing horse)
         Left as the game has them: the Chapter 1 deer skinned with Charles, the legendary
         alligator, all prompts and hold times, loot contents.
         Not taken from the download: its one coyote skinning set for every animal (large pelts
         became medium pelts and got lost), its carryconfigdata.meta and prompts.meta, and its
         scenario files, which are the unrepaired files of Just Do The Thing Already.
         Not taken from Quick Loot 1.3 (../../QuickLoot): its loot flag also matched horses,
         large birds and the legendary alligator -->

    <Resources>
        <Resource>
            <FileReplacement>
                <GamePath>update:/common/data/ai/humaninteraction.meta</GamePath>
                <FilePath>humaninteraction.meta</FilePath>
            </FileReplacement>
            <FileReplacement>
                <GamePath>update:/common/data/ai/looting/lootconfigdata.meta</GamePath>
                <FilePath>lootconfigdata.meta</FilePath>
            </FileReplacement>
        </Resource>
    </Resources>
</EasyInstall>
